# Task 17 — Windows client updater deterministic failure/rollback evidence

Date: 2026-08-22
Script: `deploy/windows/update-wifimic-client.ps1`

All cases used PowerShell 5.1 `-TestMode` with isolated fake operations and a
fresh temp state root. A non-zero exit was required for every injected failure;
the updater emitted a deterministic state receipt and removed the state root.

```text
PASS bad-revision: exit=1; prior=True,enabled=True,xml=True,clean=True
PASS ambiguous-revision: exit=1; prior=True,enabled=True,xml=True,clean=True
PASS dirty-checkout: exit=1; prior=True,enabled=True,xml=True,clean=True
PASS build-failure: exit=1; prior=True,enabled=True,xml=True,clean=True
PASS endpoint-failure: exit=1; prior=True,enabled=True,xml=True,clean=True
PASS task-registration-failure: exit=1; prior=True,enabled=True,xml=True,clean=True
PASS stop-failure: exit=1; prior=True,enabled=True,xml=True,clean=True
PASS start-failure: exit=1; prior=True,enabled=True,xml=True,clean=True
PASS health-timeout: exit=1; prior=True,enabled=True,xml=True,clean=True
PASS interrupted-swap: exit=1; prior=True,enabled=True,xml=True,clean=True
PASS malformed-revision: exit=1; prior=True,enabled=True,xml=True,clean=True
Task 17 deterministic fake-operation matrix: PASS
```

Representative post-swap rollback receipt (`AfterAtomicSwap`):

```json
{"Deterministic":true,"PriorHash":"80814ad46f05d7ebad4774fdcf6b1acca39a9c4e873f0be5d5fed0634543d068","FinalHash":"80814ad46f05d7ebad4774fdcf6b1acca39a9c4e873f0be5d5fed0634543d068","PriorExecutableRestored":true,"TaskPath":"\\wifimic\\wifimic-client","TaskEnabled":true,"TaskState":"Running","TaskXmlPreserved":true,"StagingAndTransactionClean":true}
```

The receipt and matrix proved prior executable hash preservation, exact task XML
preservation, task re-enable/restart, and cleanup after failures before build,
after candidate build, during stop/start, during health, and immediately after
the atomic swap. The bad-revision and malformed-revision cases failed before
candidate build or mutation; the dirty-checkout case failed before fetch.

Revision contract probes also returned exit 1 for missing `-Tag`, a leading-space
revision, and an option-like `--bad` revision. No operation log was produced for
these textual validation failures.

## Limitations

- The fake operation matrix does not claim a real Scheduled Task `Ready`/`Running`
  result, a real binary version, or live client audio behavior.
- Read-only live inspection found the exact VB-CABLE endpoint, but the canonical
  task is intentionally absent because explicit host mutation was not authorized.
- The native path requires Windows, an interactive administrator session, and the
  explicit `-AcceptHostMutation` switch. It uses bounded `git`, `cargo`, and
  `schtasks.exe` subprocesses, same-volume temporary swap files, and no firewall
  operation.
